  "claim_short": "Let Omega be any bounded Reinhardt domain. Suppose every symbol in a finite Toeplitz product except one is bounded and separately quasihomogeneous (it has a single character under the coordinate torus). The exceptional symbol may lie at any position and may belong merely to L^2(Omega). If the product vanishes on analytic polynomials, then one of the symbols is zero almost everywhere.",
